From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dreyk <dreyksmail@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 17:37:01 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: mt76: reset operating channel survey on software scan

__mt76_set_channel() clears chan_state only when tuning to a channel
other than main_chandef.chan. As a result, a software scan (including
ACS when a radio is restarted) finds the operating channel with hours
of accumulated active, busy, TX, and BSS-RX history, while every other
channel covers only the scan dwell. Traffic from the AP's own clients
then makes the current channel look busy compared to idle channels.

In mt76_sw_scan(), take dev->mutex, fold any pending hardware counters
and elapsed time into the current state via mt76_update_survey(), and
then zero the main channel's chan_state under dev->cc_lock. On MT7615 and
MT7915, mt76_update_survey() updates the MIB/state_ts baselines before
zeroing chan_state so no counts are lost or double-counted across the
scan boundary.

Side effects on survey consumers in this image:
- LuCI (network.js / luci-bwc.c) reads only the noise floor, not channel
  active/busy times.
- collectd-mod-iwinfo reads bitrate, signal, noise, quality, and
  associated station count via libiwinfo (src/iwinfo.c), not channel
  active/busy times; when noise is absent it submits 0.
- hostapd BSS Load is on (bss_load_update_period defaults to 60 in the
  wifi-scripts schema). hostapd takes a utilization sample only when
  channel_time and channel_time_busy grow, so the interval that spans a
  reset gives no sample, and the next one counts from the new values.
- usteer is not in the image.
- After the reset, state->noise is 0 so the in-use channel omits
  SURVEY_INFO_NOISE_DBM ("noise:") until the next mt76_update_survey().
  On wl0 (2.4 GHz, mt7615e), mt76_get_survey() and mt7615_mac_work()
  (every 100 ms) refresh it immediately once on channel (measured 4 ms
  after scan trigger on ch 1; absent only while off-channel during scan).
  On wl1 (5 GHz, mt7915e), mt7915_phy_get_nf() returns 0 so "noise:"
  is already absent at rest and across 9 s post-scan.
---
 mac80211.c | 13 +++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 13 insertions(+)

diff --git a/mac80211.c b/mac80211.c
index 7d27f952..7755e71b 100644
--- a/mac80211.c
+++ b/mac80211.c
@@ -1963,6 +1963,19 @@ void mt76_sw_scan(struct ieee80211_hw *hw, struct ieee80211_vif *vif,
 		  const u8 *mac)
 {
 	struct mt76_phy *phy = hw->priv;
+	struct mt76_dev *dev = phy->dev;
+
+	mutex_lock(&dev->mutex);
+	mt76_update_survey(phy);
+	if (phy->main_chandef.chan) {
+		struct mt76_channel_state *state;
+
+		state = mt76_channel_state(phy, phy->main_chandef.chan);
+		spin_lock_bh(&dev->cc_lock);
+		memset(state, 0, sizeof(*state));
+		spin_unlock_bh(&dev->cc_lock);
+	}
+	mutex_unlock(&dev->mutex);
 
 	set_bit(MT76_SCANNING, &phy->state);
 }
